# Submodules format themselves with their own prettier config and their own
# pre-commit hook. Descending into them from the parent reformats content the
# parent doesn't own -- that's how we got the churn we had to restore once
# already. `pre-commit run` never sees this content either: git submodules
# are invisible to the parent's own index, so `plugins/**` files never reach
# the parent's pre-commit hook. This file just teaches the bare `prettier`
# CLI (which walks the filesystem, blind to submodule boundaries) the same
# boundary pre-commit already gets for free from git.

# Node tooling, if ever installed locally for pinning (see Makefile
# `prettier-check`/`prettier-fix`).

.kiwee/
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
node_modules/

# Tool-written or test data: a reformat would be undone by the tool or change a test.
assets.lock.json
cloudyreader/data/*.json
tests/golden/*.yaml

# Jekyll templates hold Liquid, which Prettier rewrites and breaks.
docs/_includes/
docs/_layouts/
docs/404.html
docs/assets/
docs/_sass/

# npm writes these with its own layout; the 4-space JSON rule of .prettierrc fails them.
site/package.json
site/package-lock.json
